{"kind":"request","text":"Please review J4 setup Source V10 for adoption. It answers your changes requested in d69d6964. Both files below are frozen. If either changes, the review no longer applies.\n\nEvidence body SHA-256: 4997254d95a969fc64becd11203ed7216b37c0d3c3fdedce4bdd3600a4730717\nOperator Source SHA-256: f08e6b40f28c5ebd71f852c060e5668875094f3fd0941a84bc42ee25086024d1\n\nSource: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-setup-equivalence-implementation-source-20261031-v10, source-index.json sha256 4fb4509d1f626fb532681e4db17b801921e45cf973b1712310ce8c208e14ba66, PINS.json sha256 c823aff2a1d4d752d62589069ee16b1f306921d4f36fb6537a76801f147eef68. Start with the V10 section of PLAN.md and v9-to-v10.patch.\n\nQualification capture: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-v15-source-qualification-checks-20261031-v2, source-filesystem-1. Receipt sha256 025e11139688f22a8a61d924e850e460aa7805e1e518eb5542d220db08ddb872, stdout sha256 b4ac23c684ff6d38ec6c12d29ded3cd480a2a9c56a5522730a100c74bff21da0. One run at 16:26 UTC, inside deny.sb: exit 0, setup-112-source-filesystem-qualified, 47 of 47 cases, 0 global network attempts, 0 private path attempts, 1,184 fixture files, Source unchanged.\n\nRehearsal capture: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-v15-rehearsal-20261031-v1/rehearsal-receipt.json, sha256 b58362fbae41edc25ffd7eaed2d5ef4e6833311317e954739ac4e46da7e158ee. One run of 186.10 s, inside rehearsal-deny.sb, which adds only loopback to deny.sb. It ran the unchanged operator.mjs from first to last original against local workerd judges and SQLite, with a stand-in provider, and classified rehearsal-complete.\n\n- clean: setup-complete, 14 originals accepted, 91 requests.\n- retries: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 95 requests. Fork answered unknown, refused, confirmed. Revoke answered unknown, confirmed.\n- head-late: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 103 requests. Head answered unknown, then confirmed on the same attempt.\n- head-unknown: native-setup-unknown, 9 accepted, 77 requests.\n- fork-spent: native-setup-unknown, 9 accepted, 77 requests.\n\nThe rehearsal proves nothing about a Worker or the real provider. It stubs sourceQualification, previous, the read floor and the execution context, and it sets the policy generation to 2 where the real room has 3. The receipt records each substitution by digest.\n\nRead-only copy of Source and captures: /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-31-j4-setup-source-v10, SHA256SUMS sha256 092f48fbfcda3c6e3ba55062327af5604b10de5fad258198e0bab20fcfc281b1. Authoring reds, stderr and any rehearsal receipts only: /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-31-j4-setup-source-v10-reds, SHA256SUMS sha256 2df8e9ac8bcdbb807a1ed12d2a2dafdaa4aae89ceae493926f7863afac3506ab. The reds ran in authoring, against this Source's text with one change each. I did not reread them or rerun them at the release roots.\n\nWhat I read: the V9 to V10 diffs of operator.mjs, setup.mjs, setup-native.mjs, safety.mjs and recovery.mjs, and rehearse-setup.mjs in full. I did not read rehearsal-worker.ts, rehearsal-preload.mjs, rehearsal-equivalence.mjs or the new qualifier cases. Since V9 I do not treat a passing qualifier as proof of what a real judge accepts, so please weigh the stand-in in rehearsal-worker.ts yourself.\n\nYour items:\n1. Definition bytes: open-issue and open-pr now carry them. A real judge refused each one without the bytes, with bad-field, in authoring rehearsals rr-issue-bytes and rr-change-bytes.\n2. Moved head: inside a poll, history-head-moved and summary-history-head-moved read again within the same bound. Outside a poll, they still stop the run. result.movedHeadReads counts them.\n3. Local clock: setup-native.mjs now compares the hold's end with the scope's own time only.\n4. Refusal words: result.halt names the original in flight and the last one accepted, with the refusal's fixed reason and name.\n5. Rehearsal: above.\n\nPlease weigh these points. The first three go beyond or against what I or you said:\na. Rule for a spent attempt. Refused on the last attempt halts at once. Unknown on the last attempt, head included, keeps reading until the window closes, then halts. My decision said to halt on exhaustion. The agent kept the reading because ledger.ts:432 lets a late own answer settle an unknown, and head-late shows that recovery. I accept this. An all-refused fork turns failed, so that halt reads native-fork-failed-or-changed.\nb. Fresh namespace. A halt after activate-issue needs more than a fresh namespace, because assertOriginalsAbsent(FIXED.vault) reads a path with no namespace. The earlier statement covers only halts before the first original is retained. So a halt after any original costs this vault as well as the room.\nc. R26. You held R26 sound, and the rehearsal found a defect there, carried from V14. Native answers a preparation with intent null, and V14 required the digest, so setup would have halted at instance-a. setup.mjs, recovery.mjs and the oracle now require null for a preparation, and the followed entry still binds the signed intent. A real judge run with the digest required halts at instance-a after 10 accepted.\nd. Time and request budget. A fork window is nine reads over 41.25 s. The worst case is 189 of 192 requests. It reaches 207 and refuses with request-bound if a history read takes a second page, which no rehearsal saw. The worst-case time of 179.43 s against the 180 s bound is inferred from 0.37 s per request, measured once on dap-demo. A slower Worker reaches command-deadline, and two 30 s hangs in one window cost the room. Is this margin acceptable for a one-try room, or should setup carry less polling?\ne. Removed check. setup-native.mjs no longer refuses a second confirmed row, because a late answer to an earlier attempt can add one. The earliest row decides, and the selected-attempt checks still follow.\nf. Fragments. Ten cases still run operator fragments or text checks, and six use the fake endpoint, whose bad-field is a copy of a rule. The rehearsal is what covers the whole operator.\n\nStale words from your point b: the names file status and PLAN.md no longer say that the two values await the planner.\n\nWhat did not run: verifyPacket, collector main, the finalizer at a real path, verifyActualReview past its first refusal, any Worker request, and any private path. Only reads R01 to R07 have proof under Worker da13242c. Most setup writes have none under that Worker, and R28 to R30 have none under any Worker. The J4 report must state this, along with the Membership window, the planner's item 10, which covers key presence and mode only, and one try per room.\n\nThe landed worktree is clean at 112eff12. Main has moved to 09420198, and no Worker has been deployed since 112eff12. A deployment before setup voids this Source.","body":{"conditions":"Review the complete operator Source V10 at the stated digests, its diff from V9, and its actual qualification and rehearsal captures, for adoption. If you approve, file a report whose first text line holds Verdict: APPROVED and which holds the two full digest lines from 82ff38c9, each exactly on its own line, with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. This review adopts the operator only. It releases no admission, read or setup, and it is not J4 or S1 completion.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2325d2bdec8bb369d6c3cd77d8163d178ccacc09, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d69d6964539f1c3423c54cc57a1d00ded1ed65f7 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d1